  "title": "Headless build for Brett across two repos in this folder: ./hub (MossesX/axHub) and ./axf (MossesX/…",
  "asked": "Headless build for Brett across two repos in this folder: ./hub (MossesX/axHub) and ./axf (MossesX/AmberX-AXF). Read each repo's CLAUDE.md + rules. Opus, one session. Git auth is in your environment (GIT_CONFIG_*); just git push. 0. AXF part: wait (poll every 30 s, max 40 min) until origin/main in ./axf contains the menu-approve build (git log origin/main --oneline | grep -i 'menu-approve\\|Waiting for approvals', or origin/claude/menu-approve is an ancestor). Do the axHub server part first while waiting. Brett: every approval just says \"vps.run\". He wants to know WHO asked and WHAT it is. 1. axHub server (./hub): record the caller on every held/confirm request: source = claude.ai (chat or voice), Claude Code, headless build, console, agent, system (vinnie), derived from the OAuth client / token used, the MCP initialize clientInfo name+version, and an optional header X-Axhub-Session (session/build/agent name, strict pattern, max 60 chars). Store it with the approval; expose it in the approvals API. Tests. 2. AXF (./axf): the console token caller and headless builds send X-Axhub-Session (console: 'console'; headless builds: their --name via env AXF_SESSION set in deploy/claude-headless.sh; agents: agent name). 3. UI in apps/axhub-web (list, the Waiting for approvals dropdown, detail page) and AmberX's hub view: each row shows Source badge (Claude.ai / Claude Code / Headless / Console / Agent / System), Who (session/build/agent name), the reason TITLE first, then the tool (vps.run) as a small chip, Requested time, countdown. Columns sortable/filterable via the framework grid. Framework controls + theme/scale tokens only. No flicker (update in place). 4. Tests + full test suites in both repos green. Commit; fetch+merge origin/main; retest; git push origin HEAD:main in both (retry until it lands). Coolify redeploys axHub from main. Short report in ./axf/_claude/builds/reports/approval-source.md.",
